 "reason": "The geometry is largely faithful and correct: the (2/sqrt c)artanh distance is the standard Poincare-ball metric for lambda_x = 2/(1-c||x||^2), the declared factor-2 amendment is consistently applied (the half-factor m_i/2 gives d_c(0,Delta_i) = m_i exactly), the Mobius formulas in displaced_code and in all four continuous_surface statements, the tangent, the 1e-12 direction guard, the coordinate-norm magnitude, the detached cap m_i = min(M_i, 0.5 d_nn_i), the balanced plan on C itself, the two switches in prose and the level-1-untouched loss are all right. But the reference executable does not compute what the mechanism declares: it builds the quantised vector from the scaled codebook (so the decoder gets E_k/q_l instead of the raw codeword), it runs the residual recursion in q_l units without detach (double-scaling level 3 and dropping the declared value chain), it rebuilds d_nn_i and Delta_i from the cost's own c (so GEOM=euclid silently changes the behaviour field, contradicting the switch), and its lift uses an eps pole guard instead of the stated tanhc zero limit. In addition the gradient path drops v_i from the differentiable surface, contrary to the idea's 'gradients flow only through v_i and u_k', without being flagged as a recorded amendment. These must be corrected before the specification is a faithful, complete and unambiguous formulation of the idea."
